    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14705" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dŏmĭto</span></b> ,
		āre, v. freq. a.
		domo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to tame</i>, <i>break in</i> (very rare; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perh. first used by Verg.): boves,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 1, 285</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quadrupedum omne genus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Manil. 4, 234</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">elephantos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					8, 8, 8, § 25</span></i>
			.—<b>Poet.</b>: currus (i. e. <i>a team</i>), <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 7,
				163</span></i>.</div>
